  "RightSideDisplay": 10,
  "RightSideHtmlBlock": "<h4>RESPOND and RECOVER outcomes this move</h4><p>For each Category, rate how far the team achieved the CSF outcome during this move. The Category statements are CSF 2.0's own; the four performance levels are this model's, not CSF's. Record what was done in the comments.</p><p>Subcategories to consider: RS.MA-01 to -05 (plan executed with third parties; reports triaged and validated; incidents categorized, prioritized, escalated); RS.AN-03, -06 to -08 (root cause; records preserved; magnitude estimated); RS.CO-02, -03 (stakeholders notified; information shared); RS.MI-01, -02 (contained; eradicated); RC.RP-01 to -06; RC.CO-03, -04 (recovery progress communicated; public updates via approved messaging).</p><p><i>Source: The NIST Cybersecurity Framework (CSF) 2.0, NIST CSWP 29 (February 26, 2024), Appendix A, RESPOND (RS) and RECOVER (RC) Categories. Public domain. CSF 2.0 says the Tiers \"characterize the rigor of an organization's cybersecurity risk governance and management practices\"; Appendix B is a \"notional illustration\". They are not maturity levels.</i></p>",
